{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>You shall not hate your brother in your heart.</b> If you heard that he wronged you, you shall not harbor hidden hatred for him in your heart, but rather <b>you shall surely rebuke</b> him — why did you do this to me? And perhaps through this the matter will become clear, that it is all a lie and he did not intend what you suppose, or he will set right what he did wrong. And through this <b>you shall not bear sin on his account</b> — to suspect him of what he is not. Another interpretation: <b>you shall surely rebuke your fellow</b> — if you saw something shameful in him, rebuke him. But if you do not rebuke him, <b>you shall bear sin on his account</b> — to suspect him of what he is not." "<b>On his account.</b> For his sake. As in <b>כי עליך הורגנו כל היום</b>, <b>כי עליך נשאתי חרפה</b>."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:30.963745846Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}